-- a crystal energy landscape: one molecule, a type of candidate solids, and the proof that each of them
-- is a solid of that molecule. This is the fiber of the solid over the molecule, which is what
-- polymorph-not-determined says is inhabited more than once, so the landscape is not an artefact of the
-- method but the situation.
Landscape : Type 1
Landscape = (M : Mol) × (I : Type 0) × (f : I → Solid) × ((i : I) → solid-mol (f i) ≡ M)
